# Testing conventions

The full **Testing** section lives in `AGENTS.md` — read it. In short:

- `pytest` with `asyncio_mode = auto`. `tests/unit/` must run without a
  database; anything needing Postgres goes in `tests/integration/` (gated by
  `INTEGRATION_TESTS=1`).
- Every functional change ships with a test. Normalization changes get a
  before/after case in `tests/unit/test_normalization.py`.
- `make lint` and `make test-unit` must pass before proposing changes.

```bash
make test-unit                            # fast, no DB
pytest tests/unit/test_clustering.py -v   # single file
make test-int                             # needs: docker compose up postgres -d
```
